  "chapter": 665,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 46 Chapter 665\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 8289, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the Indian law, in relation to non-Indian trespass\n        and drug trafficking activities within Indian lands\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill expands the ability of Indian nations to identify and  expel\nintruders  from Indian land. The bill would also allow the Seneca Nation\nto enter into agreements with law enforcement entities to enhance public\nsafety on Seneca Nation land.\n \n  The Seneca Nation has indicated that this bill is  necessary  for  the\nsafety  and wellbeing of the Seneca people. Other Indian tribes, seeking\nto enhance public safety on their lands, also have indicated support for\nthis bill. However, some ambiguities and technical issues  in  the  bill\nneeded  to  be  clarified, including concerning the nature of agreements\nbetween the Seneca Nation and local law enforcement.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with  the  legislature  to  address  these\nissues.  On the basis of that agreement, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
